[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.85]
\node[left,font=\small] at (-0.1,0.95) {Sand};
\foreach \x in {0.00,0.70,1.40,2.10} {\draw[fill=blue!15] (\x,0.65) rectangle +(0.7,0.6);}
\node[left,font=\small] at (-0.1,0.30) {Cement};
\foreach \x in {0.00,0.70,1.40,2.10,2.80} {\draw[fill=red!12] (\x,0.00) rectangle +(0.7,0.6);}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Mortar is mixed from sand and cement in the ratio $4:5$. How many parts are there in total?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.85]
\node[left,font=\small] at (-0.1,0.95) {Ravi};
\foreach \x in {0.00,0.70,1.40} {\draw[fill=blue!15] (\x,0.65) rectangle +(0.7,0.6);}
\node[left,font=\small] at (-0.1,0.30) {Ling};
\foreach \x in {0.00,0.70,1.40,2.10,2.80} {\draw[fill=red!12] (\x,0.00) rectangle +(0.7,0.6);}
\draw[decorate,decoration={brace,amplitude=5pt}] (3.75,1.25)--(3.75,0) node[midway,right=8pt,font=\small] {$\$56$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Ravi and Ling share $\$56$ in the ratio $3:5$. How much does Ravi receive?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.85]
\node[left,font=\small] at (-0.1,1.60) {Share 1};
\foreach \x in {0.00} {\draw[fill=blue!15] (\x,1.30) rectangle +(0.7,0.6);}
\node[left,font=\small] at (-0.1,0.95) {Share 2};
\foreach \x in {0.00,0.70} {\draw[fill=red!12] (\x,0.65) rectangle +(0.7,0.6);}
\node[left,font=\small] at (-0.1,0.30) {Share 3};
\foreach \x in {0.00,0.70,1.40} {\draw[fill=green!20] (\x,0.00) rectangle +(0.7,0.6);}
\draw[decorate,decoration={brace,amplitude=5pt}] (2.35,1.90)--(2.35,0) node[midway,right=8pt,font=\small] {$\$120$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\$120$ is shared in the ratio $1:2:3$. How much is the largest share?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.85]
\node[left,font=\small] at (-0.1,0.95) {Melons};
\foreach \x in {0.00,0.70,1.40,2.10,2.80,3.50,4.20} {\draw[fill=blue!15] (\x,0.65) rectangle +(0.7,0.6);}
\node[left,font=\small] at (-0.1,0.30) {Bananas};
\foreach \x in {0.00,0.70,1.40} {\draw[fill=red!12] (\x,0.00) rectangle +(0.7,0.6);}
\draw[decorate,decoration={brace,amplitude=5pt}] (5.15,1.25)--(5.15,0) node[midway,right=8pt,font=\small] {$30$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Ben buys melons and bananas in the ratio $7:3$. He buys $30$ pieces of fruit in total. How many more melons than bananas does he buy?
